
This file contains information about relationships bewteen class templates
defined in the Rp namespace (rp/ directory) and subclasses defined in the
Rpc and Rpg namespaces (rpc/ and rpg/ directories). 

A subclass defined in the Rpc or Rpg namespace is "trivial" if it does not
have any data members and does not define or override any member functions 
other than possibly a constructor.

=============================================================================
fields/

  Class templates in this directory use multiple template parameters 
  rather than a single Types class. They should all be changed to use
  a Type class.

  Mask    -> trivial
  Domain  -> trivial
  CFields -> trivial
  WFields -> nontrivial: extra setRGrid(DeviceArray function), rpc is trivial 
  FieldIo -> notrivial: differentiate read/write operations (see below)
  Domain  -> trivial (FFT, Wavelist, FieldIo)

  FieldIo  -
      Uses local host arrays DArray< HostDArray<cudaReal> >
      Use copy device <-> host using copyArrays function defined
          in field/fieldCheck. Uses overloaded "=" operator.
      Use = operator directly for single arrays

      For read operations: 
           Allocate, read on host, copy from host to device

      For write operations:
           Allocate, copy device to host, write

      Need operation that:
         On GPU, allocates outer DArray, and HostArrays
         On CPU, allocates outer DArray, not FftwDRArray objects

      Proposal:

             allocateHostArrays(DArray< arrayType >)
             allocateHostArray( arrayType )

             updateHostArrays(DArray< arrayType >)
             updateDeviceArrays(DArray< arrayType >)
             updateHostArray(DArray< arrayType >)
             updateDeviceArray(DArray< arrayType >)

             Wrap allocateArrays and "=" operator by default.
             Specialize for FftwDRArray.

             Place in field/fieldCheck

